From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PowerPC] Expand 128-bit division on 32-bit targets

PPCTargetLowering never sets the widest division it supports, so it
stays at the default and i128 sdiv, udiv, srem and urem on 32-bit
PowerPC become calls to __divti3, __udivti3, __modti3 and __umodti3.
libgcc only provides those on 64-bit targets, so anything using 128-bit
division fails to link; the Swift runtime is one, through Int128.

Limit division to 64 bits on 32-bit PowerPC, so ExpandLargeDivRem expands
wider operations inline, as ARM and 32-bit X86 already do.
---
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCISelLowering.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/PowerPC/PPCISelLowering.cpp
@@ -1409,6 +1409,11 @@
   else
     setMaxAtomicSizeInBitsSupported(32);
 
+  // libgcc has no 128-bit division routines on 32-bit targets, so expand
+  // wider division in IR there, as ARM and 32-bit X86 do.
+  if (!isPPC64)
+    setMaxDivRemBitWidthSupported(64);
+
   setStackPointerRegisterToSaveRestore(isPPC64 ? PPC::X1 : PPC::R1);
 
   // We have target-specific dag combine patterns for the following nodes:
